WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Metacognition makes learning more active.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.885
Instead of passively consuming content, the learner plans practice, monitors progress,

00:00:06.885 --> 00:00:10.560
uses retrieval, spaces review, seeks feedback, and adjusts methods.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.090
The learner asks what capability is being built and what evidence would show that the

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.120
capability is real.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.795
This keeps learning connected to performance instead of completion.

00:00:17.795 --> 00:00:21.165
Planning practice means choosing the skill and the exercise deliberately.

00:00:21.165 --> 00:00:22.945
If the goal is better troubleshooting,

00:00:22.945 --> 00:00:26.060
practice may focus on hypothesis formation or evidence collection.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.010
If the goal is better writing, practice may focus on outlining or revising claims.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.860
If the goal is better communication,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.700
practice may focus on summarizing uncertainty or asking clearer questions.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.880
Monitoring progress means noticing whether the current method is working.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.020
Are errors repeating?

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.320
Is the learner retrieving the idea without looking?

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.110
Is the task too easy, too hard, or productively challenging?

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.135
Has feedback identified a bottleneck?

00:00:47.135 --> 00:00:51.440
A metacognitive learner adjusts difficulty and strategy instead of assuming that more time

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.970
with the same method will automatically solve the problem.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.290
This also helps learners know when to ask for help.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:01:00.090
Asking for help is more effective when the learner can name the target, the attempt,

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.520
the gap, and the uncertainty.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.060
Instead of saying, I do not get it, the learner can say, I can follow the example,

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.320
but I cannot choose the method on a new problem.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.920
That is a much better starting point for useful feedback.
